# Week 3 – Password Cracking with JTR

## Project Module 1

As part of my Cybersecurity Internship at Networkwalks, I completed a hands-on password security exercise using John the Ripper (JTR) and a protected PDF provided for the lab.

## Tasks Completed

- Verified John the Ripper installation in Kali Linux
- Extracted the password hash from the protected PDF
- Saved the extracted hash for password recovery
- Used John the Ripper to perform password recovery
- Successfully recovered the PDF password
- Verified the recovered password by opening the protected PDF
- Successfully completed the provided CTF challenge and captured the flag

## Tools Used

- Kali Linux
- John the Ripper (JTR)
- pdf2john
- Protected PDF



This exercise provided practical understanding of password hashing, password recovery, dictionary-based attacks, and the importance of strong password protection.

